From 963bd30ab7614de9360a4b39598d9c1d37f68618 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: bugcheck <bugcheck@local>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 11:51:10 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 17/17] Shops: no occluder in front of an open shop room
 (interior looked empty from the door)

Yasin 7 Nov (phone screenshots, Crownado Beach Coffee): right after Open the shop looked
empty from the door; counter, machines, tables and staff appeared ~1 m inside. Cause: the
shop-street occluders (shops_layer black-dc-perf31) put one quad 0.8 m behind every shop
facade with no door hole, so occlusion culling dropped every room piece wholly behind it
until the camera passed it. While a room is live (loaded on its door's Use, freed when the
player leaves) its point 1.2 m inside the door is listed in CoronadoShopInterior.occ_holes;
the facade quad of that front (and, as a safety net, any building footprint occluder that
contains the point) is left out and comes back when the room is freed. Rendered check
(xvfb, opengl3): doorway view now shows the room's furniture (was an empty floor).
